GIMP Palette
Name: pixel-sprites-lit-diorama - example (day market)
Columns: 4
# One instance of the colour structure in style.md. Never ship it as is: every game re-chooses
# each role, and its lighting, for its own tone. demo.html's night palette fills the same roles.
# Checked against style.md's colour-rules (value = HSV V, chroma = S x V, contrast = WCAG ratio):
#   ink on plate 15.5:1; accent and signals on plate >= 5.4:1; ink and accent on the caption backing
#   (plate at 85% over white) >= 4.9:1
#   chroma of sky, fog, ground, material-* max 0.37 (ceiling 0.40); sprites max 0.58 (set + 0.21)
#   value of ground, material-* max 0.78 (ceiling 0.80); glow-lamp 1.00
#   outline V 0.14; ground - outline 0.58; outline on fog 11.8:1
#   tint V 1.00, chroma 0.08; accent chroma 0.66 (set max 0.37); accent hue >= 40 deg from every coloured set role and signal
# key, fill-sky, fill-ground and rim are the lighting scheme: no rule, the game picks them.
